 "title": "Microbiota and Diet Study in Dezhou Jennies",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around a study on the microbiota and diet of Dezhou jennies, a type of donkey. The jennies were fed yeast hydrolysate, basal diet, and MCON and MYE, resulting in higher triglyceride levels. The microbiota of the jennies consists of Arcanobacterium, Bacillota, and Bacteroidota. The study was conducted by authors, acknowledged by FAR, and published in a paper. The study was assisted by Yunnan Pulis Biotechnology Co. and involved the University of Milano-Bicocca and the Dalian Institute of Chemical Physics.",
